\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21.1.1}{\ignorespaces The canonical cover of the query range \([2..9]\) in the merge-sort tree over \(A\). It is exactly \(\{[2..2],\,t_9[3..4],\,t_5[5..8],\,[9..9]\}\) -- four nodes, no two overlapping, whose intervals tile \(2..9\). Counting values \(\le 3\) bisects each node's \emph  {sorted} list: \((2)\to 1\), \((4,5)\to 0\), \((1,1,3,5)\to 3\), \((7)\to 0\). The green arrows sum to \(4\).}}{1286}{figure.caption.232}\protected@file@percent }
