\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21.2.1}{\ignorespaces Path copying one write \(A[3]=9\) on the running array (opener's grid). Only the five nodes on the root-to-leaf path to \(t_{18}\) are \emph  {freshly cloned} (orange, \(+5\) folded into each sum: \(49{\to }54,\,24{\to }29,\,14{\to }19,\,9{\to }14,\,4{\to }9\)). Their untouched siblings (dashed gray) are \emph  {shared} with \(v_0\). Both roots stay valid trees, so reading \([1..8]\) on \(v_1\) gives \(t_2'{=}29\) while the same read on \(v_0\) still gives \(t_2{=}24\).}}{1296}{figure.caption.234}\protected@file@percent }
