\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21.3.1}{\ignorespaces The joint two-root descent for the \(k\)-th smallest of \(A[3..9]\) (\(k=4\)). At each value node the branch label is the \emph  {difference} of \(\mathit  {root}_9\)'s and \(\mathit  {root}_2\)'s left-child counts -- the number of query elements in the lower half. \(3<4\) pushes into \([4..7]\) with \(k'=1\); then \([4..5]\) holds \(3\ge 1\) elements so we take the low half and land on value \(4\). Orange = descended, gray = skipped.}}{1307}{figure.caption.236}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c19-roots}{{21.3.1}{1307}{The joint two-root descent for the \(k\)-th smallest of \(A[3..9]\) (\(k=4\)). At each value node the branch label is the \emph {difference} of \(\mathit {root}_9\)'s and \(\mathit {root}_2\)'s left-child counts -- the number of query elements in the lower half. \(3<4\) pushes into \([4..7]\) with \(k'=1\); then \([4..5]\) holds \(3\ge 1\) elements so we take the low half and land on value \(4\). Orange = descended, gray = skipped}{figure.caption.236}{}}
